  Even a 6x change in band width leaves the trial ordering almost
  identical. The metric is close to a monotone transform of itself.

========================================================================================
(3) Where does the arousal-performance association actually live?
========================================================================================

  pooled across all trials      r = +0.270 (p = 0.0003)
  WITHIN subject (centred)      r = +0.353 (p = 0.0000)
  BETWEEN subjects (means)      r = +0.190 (p = 0.4801, n = 16)

  A per-subject multiplier is a constant within a subject, so it can
  only act on the BETWEEN component. If the association is carried by
  the WITHIN component, band width has almost nothing to act on.

